---
import ContactCTA from '../components/ContactCTA.astro';
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
	title="About | Daniele Sala"
	description="Environmental engineer and hydrological researcher. M.Sc. Politecnico di Milano 106/110. Applying for a PhD on forest-water relations during drought at LIST (Luxembourg)."
>
	<div class="stack gap-20">
		<main class="wrapper about">
			<Hero
				title="About"
				tagline="Environmental engineer with a focus on process-based hydrological modelling, drought monitoring, and satellite data integration."
			/>

			<section>
				<h2 class="section-title">Research Focus</h2>
				<div class="content">
					<p>
						My research interest sits at the intersection of process-based hydrological modelling,
						multi-source data integration, and ecohydrology, specifically in the context of
						forest-water relations during drought. My M.Sc. thesis at Politecnico di Milano gave me
						hands-on experience with the central methodological challenge: constraining poorly
						identifiable sub-processes (surface runoff, interflow, deep percolation) from aggregate
						observations, using the FEST model calibrated across the Po River Basin with ten years
						of spatially distributed hydrometeorological data.
					</p>
					<p>
						I am currently applying for a PhD position at the Luxembourg Institute of Science and
						Technology (LIST), within the ForFuS interdisciplinary doctoral training unit, where I
						propose to quantify minor but mechanistically significant water pathways in forest water
						budgets during drought (foliar water uptake and forest floor evaporation) using stable
						isotopic tracers (δ¹⁸O, δ²H) and sub-canopy micrometeorological monitoring across
						experimental sites in Luxembourg, Switzerland, and the Netherlands.
					</p>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2 class="section-title">Education</h2>
				<div class="content">
					<h3>M.Sc. Environmental and Land Planning Engineering</h3>
					<p class="role-period">Politecnico di Milano · 2021–2024 · <strong>106/110</strong> (weighted avg. 27.31/30)</p>
					<p>
						Relevant coursework: Hydrogeological Risk (30/30) · Remote Sensing (30/30) ·
						Statistical Models and Stochastic Processes (29/30) · Ecosystems Conservation and Management (29/30)
					</p>
					<p>
						<strong>Master Thesis:</strong> <em>Impact of Agricultural Irrigation on the Hydrologic Regime of the Po River Basin</em><br />
						Supervisor: Prof. Giovanni Ravazzani, DICA. Developed and calibrated the FEST process-based
						hydrological model across the Po River Basin, integrating 10 years of spatially distributed
						meteorological, hydrological, and land-use data. Conducted comprehensive sensitivity and
						uncertainty analysis and built counterfactual drought scenarios isolating the contribution
						of human water-use decisions from climatic drivers. Key finding: 15% reduction in river
						flows during irrigation season (April–September), with altered evapotranspiration patterns
						and decreased aquifer levels throughout the year.
					</p>

					<h3>Erasmus Exchange Semester</h3>
					<p class="role-period">Universitat Politècnica de València (UPV), Spain · 2022–2023</p>
					<p>Specialisation in Water Quality, Pollution Transport in Natural Environments, and Wastewater Treatment Management.</p>

					<h3>B.Sc. Environmental Engineering</h3>
					<p class="role-period">Politecnico di Milano · 2018–2021</p>
					<p>Foundation in environmental engineering, fluid mechanics, hydrology, and environmental systems.</p>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2 class="section-title">Professional Experience</h2>
				<div class="content">
					<h3>Natural Risk Assessment Specialist, Progesi S.p.A.</h3>
					<p class="role-period">Milan, Italy · 2025 – Present</p>
					<p>
						Develop and maintain integrated environmental monitoring systems processing multi-source
						data from ground stations, satellite platforms, and remote sensing imagery for natural
						hazard management at regional scale. Operational use of ICON-I2 and ECMWF-IFS NWP outputs
						as meteorological forcing for regional hydrological forecasting, including calibration
						against ground-station and satellite observations over the Po Plain and Alpine foothills.
						Collaborate with university research groups and PhD teams on applied hydrometeorological
						and climate modelling projects.
					</p>
					<p>
						<strong>September 2025 Seveso &amp; Bevera flood event:</strong> Led end-to-end flood
						risk management workflow from hydrological alerting and real-time monitoring to post-event
						impact assessment and institutional reporting, supporting municipalities and Regione
						Lombardia in emergency state declarations and damage compensation claims.
					</p>

					<h3>Climate Data Analyst, Enel S.p.A.</h3>
					<p class="role-period">Milan, Italy · 2024</p>
					<p>
						Analysed climate-related datasets to assess physical and transition risks for a global
						energy infrastructure portfolio. Developed Python and R automation for climate data
						ingestion and cross-indicator sustainability benchmarking aligned with CSRD/ESRS E1.
					</p>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2 class="section-title">Skills &amp; Languages</h2>
				<div class="content">
					<p>
						<strong>Modelling &amp; computing:</strong> Python · R · MATLAB · Fortran · QGIS ·
						Remote Sensing (multispectral, UAV/drone) · GPS-based spatial surveys · SQL · Time-series analysis
					</p>
					<p>
						<strong>Hydrological tools:</strong> FEST · HEC-RAS · VIC (in progress) · ICON / ECMWF-IFS data pipelines
					</p>
					<p>
						<strong>Languages:</strong> Italian (Native) · English (C1) · Spanish (B2)
					</p>
					<p>
						<strong>Other:</strong> ENAC A1/A3 UAS Operator Certificate (Open Category)
					</p>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2 class="section-title">Academic References</h2>
				<div class="content">
					<p>
						<strong>Prof. Giovanni Ravazzani</strong>, Politecnico di Milano (DICA)<br />
						Thesis Supervisor · <a href="mailto:giovanni.ravazzani@polimi.it">giovanni.ravazzani@polimi.it</a>
					</p>
					<p>
						<strong>Prof. Marco Gianinetto</strong>, Politecnico di Milano (DICA)<br />
						Remote Sensing · <a href="mailto:marco.gianinetto@polimi.it">marco.gianinetto@polimi.it</a>
					</p>
					<p>
						<strong>Prof. Ilenia Epifani</strong>, Politecnico di Milano (DMAT)<br />
						Statistical Models and Stochastic Processes · <a href="mailto:ilenia.epifani@polimi.it">ilenia.epifani@polimi.it</a>
					</p>
				</div>
			</section>
		</main>

		<ContactCTA />
	</div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
	.about {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 3.5rem;
	}

	section {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 0.5rem;
		color: var(--gray-200);
	}

	.section-title {
		grid-column-start: 1;
		font-size: var(--text-xl);
		color: var(--gray-0);
	}

	.content {
		grid-column: 2 / 4;
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 0.75rem;
	}

	.content :global(h3) {
		font-size: var(--text-lg);
		color: var(--gray-0);
		margin-top: 1.5rem;
	}

	.content :global(h3:first-child) {
		margin-top: 0;
	}

	.role-period {
		font-size: var(--text-sm);
		color: var(--gray-400);
		margin-top: -0.5rem;
	}

	.content :global(a) {
		text-decoration: 1px solid underline transparent;
		text-underline-offset: 0.25em;
		transition: text-decoration-color var(--theme-transition);
		color: var(--accent-regular);
	}

	.content :global(a:hover),
	.content :global(a:focus) {
		text-decoration-color: currentColor;
	}

	@media (min-width: 50em) {
		.about {
			display: grid;
			grid-template-columns: 1fr 60% 1fr;
		}

		.about > :global(:first-child) {
			grid-column-start: 2;
		}

		section {
			display: contents;
			font-size: var(--text-lg);
		}
	}
</style>
